{"results": [{"id": "FAM:SF-TMP-009", "score": 0.119, "document": "# FAM:SF-TMP-009 | Study family SF-TMP-009: PULL_UP exposure-effect diagnostics\n- observed_research_question: PULL_UP exposure-effect diagnostics\n- auto_outcome_status: artifact\n- observed_hypothesis: The PULL_UP-specific decline with exposure is defensive adaptation rather than shooter selection/lineup artifact.\n- observed_result: With lineup FE: slope holding shot fixed -0.0255 (0.0061); shooter's earlier scored -0.1044 vs not scored +0.0693. No lineup FE: -0.0063 (0.0036); placebo other play types -0.0075 (0.0017).\n- auto_failure_mechanism: C_artifact (apparent effect produced by a construction, selection or labelling flaw)\n- auto_limited_by: LIM:confounding\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:CONFOUNDING\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:PLACEBO_DEPENDENCE\n- observed_failure_evidence: Effect shrinks from -0.0255 to -0.0063 without lineup FE and the same-shooter placebo on other play types is -0.0071/-0.0075, consistent with shooter-level confound.\n- observed_sample_and_power: NOT_RECORDED\n- observed_verdict: artifact_found"}, {"id": "FAM:SF34", "score": 0.116, "document": "# FAM:SF34 | Study family SF34: Opponent lineup adaptation: shot mix when opposing rim big is off floor\n- observed_research_question: Opponent lineup adaptation: shot mix when opposing rim big is off floor\n- auto_outcome_status: inconclusive\n- observed_hypothesis: Offenses attack the rim more when the opponent has no big on the floor.\n- observed_result: [CHT-075] DRIVE +0.82pp (SE 0.25 t=+3.3); POST_UP +0.43pp (SE 0.18 t=+2.4); 3PA -1.79pp (SE 0.31 t=-5.8); rim <=4ft +0.12pp (t=+0.4); PPP +0.008 (SE 0.007 t=+1.1).\n- observed_result: [TMP-020] rim_pct 0 bigs +0.123 (SE 0.295); tpa_pct -1.785 (SE 0.309); is_DRIVE +0.821 (SE 0.250); pts +0.008 (SE 0.007).\n- auto_failure_mechanism: none (no failure recorded)\n- auto_limited_by: LIM:small_sample\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER\n- observed_failure_evidence: [CHT-075] Sub-1pp mix shifts with PPP t=+1.1; chat verdict WEAK/SMALL, will not carry a paper.\n- observed_failure_evidence: [TMP-020] Rim share +0.123 with SE 0.295.\n- observed_sample_and_power: [CHT-075] N=1.07M possessions"}, {"id": "FAM:SF38", "score": 0.102, "document": "# FAM:SF38 | Study family SF38: Defensive in-game adaptation to repeated play type (exposure slope)\n- observed_research_question: Defensive in-game adaptation to repeated play type (exposure slope)\n- auto_outcome_status: inconclusive\n- observed_hypothesis: An action gets less effective the more often the defense has already seen it in the game.\n- observed_result: [CHT-065] League-wide within-game -0.0019 PPP/exposure (SE 0.0019); across-game +0.0004 (SE 0.0015); H1 exposures to H2 -0.0000 (SE 0.0024). After 5 exposures, effects >~0.02 ruled out. Only PULL_UP within-game -0.030 SE [cut; read_family for the full text]\n- observed_result: [TMP-008] Linear slope Spec A -0.0019 (0.0019), Spec B +0.0004 (0.0015); only PULL_UP survives Holm (B -0.0243 (0.0061), holm 0.0004); team trait split-half r +0.008, season-to-season +0.037.\n- auto_failure_mechanism: none (no failure recorded)\n- auto_limited_by: LIM:insufficient_exposure\n- auto_limited_by: LIM:label_or_classification_error\n- auto_limited_by: LIM:low_measurement_reliability"}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPS-058", "score": 0.1, "document": "# FAM:SF-APPS-058 | Study family SF-APPS-058: Observed on-ball defensive scheme labels (ORL-DET G1)\n- observed_research_question: Observed on-ball defensive scheme labels (ORL-DET G1)\n- auto_outcome_status: untestable\n- observed_hypothesis: NBA matchup/PBP fields can label on-ball coverage (DROP/ICE/SWITCH) at usable rates.\n- observed_result: DET: 67 on-ball HC poss, 10 labeled (14.9%) ? DROP n=5 PPP=1.20, ICE_CANDIDATE n=5 PPP=0.80, OTHER n=57 PPP=1.42. ORL: 60 poss, 2 labeled (3.3%). switches_on unpopulated.\n- auto_failure_mechanism: A_unanswerable (question not answerable with the data or design)\n- auto_limited_by: LIM:label_or_classification_error\n- auto_limited_by: LIM:small_sample\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:LABEL_ERROR\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER\n- observed_failure_evidence: Confident label rates 14.9% and 3.3%; NBA matchups feed did not populate switches_on.\n- observed_sample_and_power: n=67/60 possessions, 10/2 labeled\n- auto_validation_status: no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED\n- observed_verdict: failed_gate"}], "n_results": 4}

Stage 2. Using the retrieval result above (follow-up tools are allowed within the tool budget), complete steps 4 to 9
and reply with the final action. Output schema (all fields required):
{
 "research_concepts": [
  "concept"
 ],
 "methodological_questions": [
  "question"
 ],
 "historical_evidence": [
  {
   "id": "identifier of a record returned by a tool",
   "status_as_recorded": "outcome status exactly as stated in the record (supported | rejected | inconclusive | untestable | artifact | not a hypothesis test | no result recorded)",
   "finding": "what the record states, in its own terms"
  }
 ],
 "failed_approaches": [
  {
   "id": "identifier of a returned record",
   "what_failed": "approach",
   "why": "failure mechanism or limitation as recorded"
  }
 ],
 "evidence_establishes": [
  "what the retrieved evidence establishes for this question"
 ],
 "evidence_does_not_establish": [
  "what it leaves open or cannot show"
 ],
 "own_inferences": [
  "your inference, not stated in any record"
 ],
 "uncertainties": [
  "uncertainty or missing information"
 ],
 "historical_effect": {
  "changed_decision": "yes | no | no_historical_evidence",
  "explanation": "whether and how the historical evidence changed the decision"
 },
 "testability": {
  "p_testable": "number in [0,1]: probability the question can be answered with the stated data at useful power",
  "blocking_constraints": [
   {
    "code": "one of RISK_CODES",
    "text": "string"
   }
  ]
 },
 "prior_work": {
  "already_answered": "yes | partly | no | unknown",
  "cited": [
   "identifiers of prior work relied on"
  ],
  "summary": "string"
 },
 "risks": [
  {
   "code": "one of RISK_CODES",
   "text": "string"
  }
 ],
 "predicted_outcome": {
  "supported": "probability",
  "rejected": "probability",
  "untestable": "probability",
  "artifact": "probability",
  "uncertain": "probability"
 },
 "decision": "proceed | proceed_with_changes | do_not_proceed",
 "design": {
  "estimand": "string",
  "unit": "string",
  "sample": "string",
  "power": "string",
  "controls": "string",
  "falsification": "string",
  "multiplicity": "string",
  "decision_rule": "string",
  "data_version": "string"
 }
}
Field guidance:
- historical_evidence and failed_approaches: only records returned by a tool, with the status as recorded; empty lists
  if nothing relevant was returned.
- testability.p_testable: probability that the question can be answered with the stated data at useful statistical power.
- prior_work.already_answered: whether retrieved earlier work already answered substantially the same question.
  Use "unknown" if no earlier work was retrieved. List identifiers you relied on in prior_work.cited.
- predicted_outcome: probabilities (summing to 1) of what a competent test of the question as posed would conclude:
  supported, rejected (adequately powered null), untestable (cannot be tested with this data), artifact (apparent
  effect produced by a flaw), uncertain (inconclusive or inadequately tested).
- decision: proceed, proceed_with_changes (state the changes in design), or do_not_proceed.
- design: a pre-registration-quality plan even if the decision is do_not_proceed (then describe the minimum viable test).
